[19.89, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\n  >_ \u001b[1mOpenAI Codex\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m (v0.160.0)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[2m~/demo/worktrees/demo/1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n  permissions: \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1mYOLO mode\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  You rang? Metaphorically. You typed.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[2m\r\n\u203a \u001b(B\u001b[mFix the task CLI: --status open and --status done currently return every task. Run the existing unittest suite first  \u001b[10;1H  to reproduce it, implement filtering without modifying the input list, add an empty-list regression test, and rerun   \u001b[11;1H  tests. Show the real CLI output for --status open and a concise git diff. Do not commit.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n\u2022 \u001b(B\u001b[mI\u2019ll run the existing tests first, check repository visibility, then fix the status filter and verify the CLI output  \u001b[15;1H  without committing.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[1m\r\n\u2022\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1mRan\u001b(B\u001b[m pwd; rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*test*' -g '*task*' -g 'pyproject.toml' -g 'README*'; git remote -v; git statu\u2026\u001b[2m\u001b[18;1H  \u2514 tasks.py\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n    origin    mini:~/demo"]
