[35.311, "o", "/origin.git\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[2m\u001b[16;1H    true\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n    + 9 lines (ctrl+t to expand)                                                                                        \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[18;1H\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n\u2022 \u001b(B\u001b[mThe existing suite reproduces the bug: both status tests fail because all three tasks are returned. The origin is a   \u001b[20;1H  bare repository on your SSH host with no public hosting remote configured, so no public issue is needed. I\u2019ll add     \u001b[21;1H  filtering plus regressions for empty input and preserving the input list.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[2m\r\n\u25e6\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2mWorking\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m(19s \u2022 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1mesc\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m to interrupt)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[1m\r\n\u203a\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2mAsk Codex to do anything\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  GPT-6.1-Sol low \u00b7 ~/demo/worktrees/demo/1 \u00b7 Fix task CLI status filtering\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m?\u001b(B\u001b[m for shortcuts\u001b[78X\u001b[78C\u26a0 1 warning \u00b7 \u001b[1mf2\u001b(B\u001b[m to view \u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[26;3H"]
